= July 2024 — Released before the paperwork

**Marcin Romanowski**, a former deputy justice minister and PiS deputy, is
detained over the Justice Fund: a compensation fund for crime victims that was
distributed, according to the charges, to organisations selected for their
politics rather than their applicants. The Sejm had waived his parliamentary
immunity.

He is released within hours. Nobody in the prosecution chain had checked that
he also holds immunity as a member of the Parliamentary Assembly of the
Council of Europe, which the Sejm cannot waive. The substance of the case is
untouched. The competence of the people running it is not.

[? if left_in_government = 1: The prosecution service answers to a ministry
inside this coalition, so the failure is administratively ours whatever we
think of the case.?][? if left_in_government = 0: We hold no justice
portfolio, and the temptation is to enjoy a rival government's procedural
collapse at the expense of a case we want prosecuted.?]

- @romanowski_procedure
- @romanowski_fund
- @romanowski_attack
- @romanowski_chamber

@romanowski_procedure
title: Demand a written procedure for immunity checks before any arrest
subtitle: Protects the case from becoming a story about its own investigators; concedes the news cycle entirely.
on-arrival: {!
Q.romanowski_response = "Procedural repair";
Q.prosecution_command_clarity =
    (Number(Q.prosecution_command_clarity) || 0) + 10;
Q.prosecution_oversight_capacity =
    (Number(Q.prosecution_oversight_capacity) || 0) + 3;
Q.institutional_trust = (Number(Q.institutional_trust) || 0) + 5;
Q.judicial_legitimacy = (Number(Q.judicial_legitimacy) || 0) + 3;
Q.administrative_capacity = (Number(Q.administrative_capacity) || 0) +
    (Q.left_in_government ? 2 : 0);
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) + 1;
Q.news_headline =
    "A written immunity check becomes a precondition for every detention";
!}

One page, binding on every prosecutor: before a detention involving any
office-holder, the immunity list is checked and the check is signed. It is an
insultingly basic requirement, which is the point — the case was lost to a
box nobody ticked.

It buys no headlines and it protects the only thing that matters here, which
is that the Justice Fund file survives contact with a defence lawyer. Every
subsequent stage of this case will be tried under it.

- @poland_event_queue: Issue the immunity procedure

@romanowski_fund
title: Take the Justice Fund itself to the audit chamber and the victims
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Moves the story from one deputy to the money and the applicants who were refused.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: No research capacity is free to reconstruct the fund's grant history.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; romanowski_response = "Fund publication"; justice_fund_salience += 10; nik_independence += 4; institutional_trust += 4; public_trust += 4; administrative_reform_pressure += 3; pis_relation -= 7; media_capacity += 3; news_headline = "The Justice Fund's refused applicants are put on the public record"

We stop discussing the arrest and start publishing the grants: which victim
support organisations applied, which were refused, which received money for
purposes unrelated to victims, and which parish, foundation or association
received a fire engine instead. The audit chamber gets a formal request.

It is the version of this scandal that reaches people who do not care which
deputy was detained. It is also slower than the case, and it will still be
producing findings long after the courts have decided whether anybody is
guilty of anything.

- @poland_event_queue: Publish the fund's grant record

@romanowski_attack
title: Use the failed arrest to attack the government's justice ministry
subtitle: Available in or out of government; it makes the coalition's competence the story and the fund's victims the footnote.
on-arrival: prosecution_command_clarity -= 4; justice_fund_salience -= 4; ko_relation -= 6; left_poll_momentum += 0.15; public_trust -= 1; institutional_trust -= 3; pis_relation += 2; news_headline = "The Left turns the botched detention into a competence charge"

Eight months of promising a repaired prosecution service ended with a suspect
walking out of a building because nobody read a list. We say so, repeatedly,
and the ministry has no answer that is not an excuse.

PiS says the same thing from the other side, and by the weekend the Justice
Fund is being discussed as a story about a failed arrest rather than about
money taken from crime victims. That framing survives; the fund's applicants
do not reappear in it.

- @poland_event_queue: Press the competence charge

@romanowski_chamber
title: Put the whole Justice Fund under a statutory audit
subtitle: Requires an open referral channel. The fund outlives the defendant; the audit outlives the government.
choose-if: nik_referral_channel = 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no channel into the Supreme Audit Office, and the fund's grant history is held by the ministry being investigated.
on-arrival: romanowski_response = "Fund audit"; justice_fund_salience += 16; nik_government_hostility += 5; institutional_trust += 6; administrative_reform_pressure += 4; public_trust += 4; prosecution_oversight_capacity += 2; media_capacity += 2; pis_relation -= 6; news_headline = "The Justice Fund's entire grant history goes to the audit chamber"

Every grant since the fund was created, with the applicant, the assessment
score, the decision and the disbursement. The chamber can compel the files; a
committee can only ask for them and be refused politely.

It is the version of this that survives the defendant leaving the country,
which nobody in the room yet knows he is going to do. When he does, the case
against the fund continues without him because it was never only about him.

- @poland_event_queue: Refer the whole fund

